        "content": "Read one document and report what it says in answer to a question. Use only this document: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no guesses.\n\nQuestion: Which league does Nõmme Kalju FC play in?\n\nDocument:\n**Breaking News: Estonian Football Club Shocks Sports World by Joining NCAA Division I Men's Basketball League**\n\nIn a stunning move that has left the sports community reeling, Nõmme Kalju FC, a professional association football club from Estonia, has announced its decision to join the NCAA Division I men's basketball league in the United States. The news, which was confirmed by the NCAA and Nõmme Kalju FC officials yesterday, marks a historic moment in the world of sports, as it is the first time a European football club has joined a top-tier American college sports league. \"We are thrilled to welcome Nõmme Kalju FC to the NCAA Division I men's basketball family,\" said NCAA President, Mark Emmert, in a statement. \"Their unique blend of European flair and athletic prowess will undoubtedly bring a new level of excitement to our league.\" Nõmme Kalju FC, which has won several domestic titles in Estonia, including the Meistriliiga championship, has been looking to expand its reach beyond European borders. According to sources close to the club, the decision to join the NCAA was motivated by a desire to tap into the vast talent pool of American college basketball players. \"We believe that our football background will bring a new dimension to the game of basketball,\" said Nõmme Kalju FC's chairman, Kuno Tehva, in an exclusive interview. \"Our players are known for their technical skill and physical fitness, which we believe will translate well to the basketball court.\" The club has already begun recruiting top American college players, with several high-profile signings expected to be announced in the coming weeks. According to sources, Nõmme Kalju FC has been in talks with several top-ranked NCAA programs, including Duke, Kentucky, and North Carolina. While some have expressed skepticism about the move, citing the vastly different rules and styles of play between football and basketball, others see it as a bold and innovative step forward for the sport. \"This is a game-changer for college basketball,\" said ESPN analyst, Jay Bilas. \"Nõmme Kalju FC's entry into the NCAA will bring a level of international flair and competition that we've never seen before. It's going to be fascinating to watch.\" The club is expected to begin play in the NCAA Division I men's basketball league in the 2023-2024 season, with its home games to be played at the University of Maryland's Xfinity Center.\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"relevant\": true, \"cards\": [{\"entity\": \"\", \"sense\": \"\", \"answer\": \"\", \"as_of\": \"\", \"claim_kind\": \"\", \"attributed_to\": \"\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"claim\": \"\"}]}\n\n\"relevant\": false if the document is about some other topic and is of no use for the question; then \"cards\" is [].\n\"cards\": one card for each answer the document itself gives to the question. Usually that is one card. It is several cards if the document gives several answers, such as a list of names: one card each. It is [] if the document gives no answer. The question may fit several things that share a name: whichever of them this document is about, report its answer. If the document only says that some answer is wrong, write no card for that answer.\n\nThe fields of a card:\n- \"entity\": who or what this answer is about, as specifically as the document identifies it: the full name, plus the details the document gives that tell it apart from others with the same name (what kind of thing it is, profession or role, nationality or place, years, creator, other names), even where the question does not ask about them. At most about 25 words.\n- \"sense\": which event, edition, version, condition, place or measure the answer refers to, if the document says; otherwise \"not stated\".\n- \"a